# PIPELINE WORKFLOW RULES: TRELLIS 2 + RIGNET + GRAIL -> the game (tools/modelos)
#
# When the user provides a URL to a 3D asset (.glb) from Hugging Face (TRELLIS 2, RigNet) or GRAIL:
# 1. NEVER ask the user to download or re-upload files through the tablet.
# 2. Find the inventory id of the object: python3 tools/modelos/modelos.py estado (pending models by priority),
#    or python3 tools/assets/inventario.py faltan <category>.
# 3. Run in the Codespace terminal (it can reach huggingface.co):
#      python3 tools/modelos/modelos.py traer <ID> --url "<URL>" --fuente trellis2 --girar 90
#    (the old command still works: python3 tools/fetch_pipeline_asset.py --url "<URL>" --name "<ID or NAME>" --category "<CATEGORY>" [--animated])
# 4. Look at it in the game: cmake --build build && cmake -E copy_directory assets build/assets, then from build/:
#      xvfb-run -a ./estepa --ver <ID> --frames 40 --screenshot ver.png
#    If the front does not face the camera, run traer again with another --girar and --reemplazar.
# 5. Commit the GLB, assets/inventario.tsv, docs/INVENTARIO.md and arte/modelos/models_manifest.json, and report.

## Workflow Enforcement

### Rule 1: Automatic Asset Acquisition
- 3D assets come in through `tools/modelos/modelos.py traer` (or its wrapper `tools/fetch_pipeline_asset.py`).
- No manual downloads or uploads through the tablet interface.
- Sources: Hugging Face (TRELLIS 2, RigNet) and GRAIL; or a local GLB with `--archivo`.

### Rule 2: The inventory is the manifest
- Every model has a fixed path from its id in `assets/inventario.tsv`: `assets/models/<category>/<sub>/<name>.glb`.
  A GLB anywhere else in `assets/models/` fails CI. Never write `assets/models/<name>.glb` by hand.
- `traer` converts the high-res source to the game style (low-poly under `tris_max`, flat colors, the inventory
  size, front +X, origin at the base), marks the id `importado` and records the provenance (url, sha256, options)
  in `arte/modelos/models_manifest.json`. High-res sources stay in `arte/modelos/fuentes/` (not in git).

### Rule 3: Rigged and animated models
- People, animals and mechanisms need a skeleton and the mandatory clips of `docs/ANIMACIONES.md`; without them CI
  fails. `traer` leaves their low-poly version in `arte/modelos/para_riggear/` for RigNet; the rigged GLB comes in
  with `traer <ID> --archivo <file> --riggeado` (or `--animated` in the wrapper).
- The engine already loads every model and its clips by name (`src/world/props.c`): do NOT change C code to
  register a model or an animation.

### Rule 4: Verification & Reporting
- `python3 tools/modelos/modelos.py check` (triangles, size, base, textures) must pass, plus the checks below.
- Show the user the `--ver` screenshot and report what was imported.

## Branches: always from the latest main (no more build breaks from stale branches)
The red CI runs and crashes of PRs #114 and #115 came from branches that were behind `main` or were pushed
without the full checks (the camp read from JSON with cJSON and `anim_system`, the vegetation that crashed on the
first frame, models saved in the wrong path). To keep that from happening again:

1. **Start every task from the latest `main`**, never from another feature branch or an old local copy:
   ```bash
   git fetch origin
   git switch -c <task-branch> origin/main
   ```
   One task per branch. Keep it short-lived (merged within a day or two) and never build a branch on top of
   another branch that is not merged yet: if you need something that only exists in another branch, wait until
   it is in `main`.
2. **Before every push, bring `main` in and rebuild from scratch:**
   ```bash
   git fetch origin && git merge origin/main   # on conflicts, what is already in main wins: re-apply your change on top
   rm -rf build && cmake -S . -B build -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release && cmake --build build
   ```
   Then run every check listed in "Project Conventions" again, the reference saves
   (`cd build && xvfb-run -a ./estepa --probar-partidas ../tests/partidas`) and a screenshot. A stale `build/`
   folder hides errors: CI always configures from zero. In Codespaces, install what CI installs first:
   `sudo apt-get install -y libx11-dev libxrandr-dev libxinerama-dev libxcursor-dev libxi-dev libgl1-mesa-dev libgl1-mesa-dri xvfb ninja-build`.
3. **The code must build on the three platforms CI builds** (Linux with gcc, Windows with MSVC, Android with the
   NDK's clang):
   - plain C11: no variable-length arrays (MSVC rejects them), no GNU extensions (`typeof`, statement
     expressions, `__attribute__`), no POSIX-only headers (`unistd.h`, `dirent.h`) in `src/`, no `M_PI`
     (use the `PI` constants already in the code);
   - zero new warnings (`-Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic` on gcc, `/W4` on MSVC): what is a warning on one compiler is
     often an error on another;
   - shaders must also run on Android (GLSL ES 100, OpenGL ES 2).
4. **New files and dependencies:**
   - every new `.c` file goes into `CMakeLists.txt` (`src/sim/` in `estepa_sim`; `src/game/`, `src/world/` and
     `src/ui/` in the game sources). The Android APK builds from the same file (`tools/android/build_apk.sh`);
   - no new external libraries (cJSON or any other): the build only fetches raylib. If one is really needed,
     ask the user first.
5. **Never break what is already in `main`:** before renaming or removing a function, a struct field or a file,
   `git grep` every use and fix them all in the same commit (`src/main.c`, `src/game/`, `tests/`). When merging
   `main`, do not undo its recent changes: `git diff origin/main...HEAD --stat` must list only the files of
   your task.
6. **Pull requests:** never push to `main` directly. Open a PR from your branch, wait until the CI is green on
   Linux, Windows and Android, and only then merge. If the CI turns red, fix it on that same branch before
   anything else, and never start a new branch on top of a red one.

## GLOBAL AI BEHAVIOR RULE
- The write_to_file tool is STRICTLY UNAVAILABLE and unsupported in this workspace.
- To create, write, or modify ANY file, you MUST exclusively use the editor tool.
- Never attempt to call write_to_file under any circumstances: it triggers an AI_NoSuchToolError and wastes context tokens.

## Project Conventions (read before changing C code)
- The project conventions live in `.claude/skills/estepa/SKILL.md` and `docs/ARQUITECTURA.md`: pure C rules in `src/sim/` (tested in `tests/test_main.c`), raylib glue in `src/game/`, fixed arrays (no per-frame allocation), all UI text through `T()`/`N_()`.
- Never remove or rename a field of a shared struct (for example `Camp` in `src/world/camp.h`, used by `main.c`, the fire, combat and migration code) without updating every use. Extend structs by adding fields at the end.
- Saved structs: after changing one, run `python3 tools/save/esquema.py`; enums only grow at the end (`docs/PARTIDAS.md`).
- Before every push, all of these must pass locally (CI runs the same on Linux, Windows and Android):
```bash
cmake --build build && ./build/sim_tests
python3 tools/assets/i18n.py extraer && python3 tools/assets/i18n.py check
python3 tools/assets/inventario.py check && python3 tools/assets/inventario.py doc --verificar
python3 tools/assets/animaciones.py check && python3 tools/assets/animaciones.py doc --verificar
python3 tools/assets/iconos.py check
python3 tools/save/esquema.py check
python3 tools/modelos/modelos.py check && python3 tools/modelos/test_modelos.py
```
- Never push a commit that does not build: a red CI blocks every release.
- A build that compiles can still crash: run the game before pushing (`cmake -E copy_directory assets build/assets`, then from `build/`: `xvfb-run -a ./estepa --frames 60 --screenshot shot.png` on Linux) and look at the screenshot.
- raylib: never pass a `Material` made with `{ 0 }` to `DrawMesh`/`DrawMeshInstanced` (its `maps` is NULL: the game crashes on the first frame; use `LoadMaterialDefault()` once); `LoadShaderFromMemory(vsCode, fsCode)` takes the vertex shader first; never load shaders, meshes or materials inside the frame loop. Vegetation lives in `src/sim/flora.*` (rules, tested) and `src/world/vegetation.*` (drawing with rlgl).
